details:
When trying to create a custom editor to edit a DataList, defaults I created for said datalist bug out when ever I compile. This bug exists in the 2022 sdk and the 2019 sdk. The method I use is having a string json that I deserialized into a string, edit the values of said datalist, then reserialize it back into a json, so that when the code is life it can deserilize from that json for use in game. For elements within that DataList, to establish blank elements I'd use hardcoded datalist stuctured as such:

DataList defaultData = new DataList(new DataToke[]{

value, value, ...etc

});

However, each time I edit the code and compile, the values within the hardcoded datalist become unreadable (mainly the referenced ones). In my main project, this also effected if I had DataLists in the DataLists.  I'll link a pastebin that has example code which can recreate the issue. Create an object in an empty scene and attach the TestObj component. Then after it loads, edit the code, save, and recompile. Then reset the component and it will give the error found at the bottom of the pastebin

https://pastebin.com/BduzrdP8

Also to add, If you restart the project then the error goes away, until you compile the code again.
